Falsifies `file_allocation_table::boot_sector::verification::the_small_fat32_reading_differs_only_under_the_floor`.

The defect: the small FAT32 reading no longer checks the layout, so it takes every volume as
FAT32. A FAT16 volume the strict reading accepts would then be read with 32-bit table entries and a
root directory at a cluster number its `BPB` never stated.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(strict, Err(ParseError::LayoutContradictsClusterCount))`.

diff --git a/src/boot_sector.rs b/src/boot_sector.rs
--- a/src/boot_sector.rs
+++ b/src/boot_sector.rs
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@
         table_sectors_16,
         root_entries,
     );
-    if options.small_fat32 && fat32_layout {
+    if options.small_fat32 {
         return Ok(FileAllocationTableType::Fat32);
     }
     if !layout_agrees(counted, table_sectors_16, root_entries) {
